  "description": "What if your AI could step onto the pitch and outplay its opponent? Conv-Cup ’26: FIFA of AI is a fun, beginner-friendly AI competition where you build an autonomous football agent and put it to the test in a deterministic 2D soccer arena. Your AI will have to move, chase the ball, navigate obstacles, intercept opponents, make smart kicks, defend its goal, and—most importantly—score! Format: Team Size: 2–4 Participants 1 Core Problem Statement: Build an Ai Soccer Agent Develop and Test Your Agent Using the Provided Simulator Submit Your Agent for Head-To-Head Evaluation Matches Matches Use Different Random Seeds and Obstacle Layouts Final Results Are Determined by Goals Scored Rules: All Teams Use the Same Game Engine and Fixed Parameters Agents May Act only Through the Prescribed Interface Direct Modification of The Simulator/game State Is Prohibited External Ap Is Are Not Allowed Hidden Seeds May Be Used During Evaluation Attempts to Manipulate the Evaluation System May Result in Disqualification Eligibility: Teams of 2–4 Open to all Prizes: ₹6,000 | ₹3,000 | ₹1,500 Think. Code. Compete. Score.",
